+NOTES: str = (
+    "Section 1.2 fixes the native definition: f is a polynomial over F_p, "
+    "field elements use representatives 0,...,p-1, and an observation s_t "
+    "obeys min_z |s_t-f(t)-zp| <= Delta at a point in [-h,h]. The same "
+    "section explains the easy/non-identifiable regime h^k <= Delta and the "
+    "need to know the coefficients below degree k. Here k=1 and f(0)=0 is "
+    "public. Theorem 9 is the Step-0 discriminator: for fixed degree and "
+    "h^k > Delta*p^epsilon it gives deterministic polynomial-time recovery "
+    "from random short-interval samples via the fixed-dimensional exact CVP "
+    "algorithm of Lemma 7. Thus this module is Track B, never Track A. The "
+    "structured sample subfamily does not invoke Theorem 9's randomness. "
+    "Section 5.2 supplies the discrete-difference operator and the identity "
+    "d(x)=sum_i D^i d(0) binom(x,i), which is the compact route used here. "
+    "The certificate coefficients and its useful step are sampled first. All "
+    "progressions have the same shape and every individual error is drawn "
+    "from the same 0..Delta range; only a higher-order common-error correlation "
+    "marks the useful progression. Magnitude, first-step, zero-noise, sparse-" 
+    "monomial, and random-certificate attacks are measured. The generic exact "
+    "decoder succeeds, as Track B requires, and is reported separately."
