codex
The first adversary run caught a real construction bug: a magnitude outlier recovered the answer on 8/8 seeds. The cause is exact—not statistical noise—the no-wrap coefficient choice forced the useful progression’s residues to stay small while decoys wrapped across the field. I’m replacing that with an equivalent inverse construction that samples the useful progression’s residues across the full field first and derives the polynomial by forward differences. That preserves the certificate-by-construction property while equalizing the visible magnitude distribution.
apply patch
