The corrected candidate language has 56,689,952 structured certificates at the shipping preset—not the prior \(p^6\)-scale claim—and the demo has exactly 3 valid answers among 27 candidates. A 200,000-sample check produced 0 hits. The stronger exact decoder now takes tens of millions of counted field operations per instance; I’m running the full eight-seed adversary/baseline panel next.
The existing design is retained as a native Track-B noisy interpolation family, but its G4 prior was invalid. The certificate language and sampler now condition on one progression’s public noise bands, and the shipping noise radius has been increased so the corrected density clears the gate.
