   140	| G5 | pass | shipping density 0/200,000; reference 44,291,118 ops, 4.05 s total |
   141	| G6 | pass | four attacks 0/8 each; reference decoder 8/8 |
   142	| G7 | pass | doubling `n` from 32 to 64 grows observations 193 to 385 and still verifies |
   143	| G8 | pass | 60/60 reorder/reflection invariance checks, 60/60 carried witnesses, 20/20 distinct unrelated keys |
   144	| G9 | **blocked/fail** | compact route verifies; 150 chars, 8 atoms, 38 estimated tokens, 245 ops; no scored oracle attempts |
   145	
   146	The four failed G6 attacks were smallest-value-magnitude outlier selection,
   147	smallest-step constant-noise greedy recovery, 256 uniform certificate restarts,
   148	and a sparse top-monomial ansatz. An earlier generator version made the planted
   149	values artificially small and the magnitude attack solved 8/8; sampling planted
   150	residues across the full field removed that leak before this report was retained.
   151	
   152	## Oracle loop and G9 arms
   153	
   154	No oracle outcome exists yet. The bare harness wrote these script-owned error
   155	records and then correctly stopped as unreachable:
   156	
   157	| preset | seed | model | solved | why |
   158	|---|---:|---|---|---|
   159	| easy | 775365020 | OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
   160	| easy | 1794220179 | OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
   161	| easy | 1580483517 | Anthropic Claude Sonnet 5 | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
   162	| easy | 540271021 | OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra | error | OpenRouter HTTP 403 total key limit |
   163	
   164	| G9 arm | solved / scored attempts | API errors | conclusion |
   165	|---|---:|---:|---|
   166	| bare | 0 / 0 | 4 | unavailable |
   167	| structural hint | 0 / 0 | 4 | unavailable; G9(b) not passed |
   168	| placebo | 0 / 0 | 4 | unavailable |
   169	
   170	`hinted - placebo` is undefined in evidentiary terms (stored as `0.0` only
   171	because neither arm has a scored denominator). No claim about hint usefulness is
   172	made.
   173	
   174	## Use
   175	
   176	```python
   177	import importlib.util
   178	
   179	path = "results/1401.1331/gen_1401_1331.py"
   180	spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("g", path)
   181	g = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
   182	spec.loader.exec_module(g)
   183	inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **g.DIFFICULTY["easy"])
   184	text = g.render(inst)
   185	answer = g.parse_answer('<answer>' + __import__('json').dumps(inst['answer']) + '</answer>')
   186	assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
   187	```
   188	
   189	After a funded four-vendor hardening run has produced a `hardened` verdict and
   190	G9 has been patched from its transcripts, emit with:
   191	
   192	```bash
   193	bash scripts/emit.sh 1401.1331 20 easy
   194	```
   195	
   196	## Caveats
   197	
   198	The 0/200,000 guess rate concerns the explicitly bounded uniform certificate
   199	language after all public shape constraints; it is not a bound against a solver
   200	that notices the marker correlation. The marker-plus-differences route is
   201	intentionally fast and makes the family easy for any tool that automates it.
   202	The sample distribution is structured and does not inherit Theorem 9's
   203	random-point probability statement. I did not run Micciancio–Voulgaris CVP, LLL,
   204	or an optimized lattice package because the module is dependency-free; the exact
   205	signed-error decoder is the measured reference implementation. Finally, the
   206	oracle quota blocker means practical multi-model hardness—including the required
   207	hinted polarity test—is unknown. The family must not be submitted until those
   208	runs succeed and `selftest_report.json` has every gate passing.

