codex
The Track B generator is implemented and locally verified, but it is not yet shippable because OpenRouter rejected every oracle request with HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.”

Deliverables:

- [gen_1401_1331.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.1331/gen_1401_1331.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.1331/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.1331/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.1331/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.1331/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1401.1331/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1401.1331) supports Track B: Theorem 9 provides polynomial-time fixed-dimensional CVP recovery, while Section 5.2 provides the finite-difference compression used here.

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; 56,689,952-candidate shipping language.
- Demo exact count: 3 valid answers among 27.
- Reference decoder: 8/8, 237,052,436 counted operations, 43.41 seconds.
- Four adversarial heuristics: 0/8 each.
- Answer: 150 characters, 8 atoms.
- Compact route: 245 operations.
- G9 remains false because all 12 bare/hinted/placebo calls were API errors, not scored failures.
- `submit.sh` correctly refuses submission on G9.

No `REJECTED.md` was created: this is an external quota blocker, not a failure of the paper or family.
