codex
The first implementation is in place and the core identity checks exactly. The demo is genuinely hand-scale (nine evaluations, two coefficients), while the hard answer remains only two field elements. I’m running the full self-test now; the main risks I’m watching are accidental success by a cheap decoder, the worst-case compact-route operation count, and whether the exhaustive reference baseline is costly enough but still practical to measure across eight seeds.
